# What `dart pub publish` leaves out of the package.
#
# A .pubignore REPLACES .gitignore for pub in this directory (pub reads one or the other, never
# both), so everything .gitignore keeps out is repeated here first. Nested .gitignore files, such
# as example/.gitignore, still apply.

# --- Repeated from .gitignore ---
*.class
*.log
*.pyc
*.swp
.DS_Store
.atom/
.buildlog/
.history
.svn/
migrate_working_dir/
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws
.idea/
.fvm/
/pubspec.lock
**/doc/api/
.dart_tool/
.flutter-plugins-dependencies
/build/
/coverage/

# --- lamp and the owner agent: machine-local tooling, never part of the package ---
.lamp/
lamp.lock
.llm_chat/
.harbor_owner/
.claude/
CLAUDE.md

# --- Repository upkeep a package consumer has no use for ---
.github/
.vscode/
.fvmrc
tool/
doc/

# harbor_test/ is a package of its own, published from its own directory, and it is NOT listed
# here: pub applies these rules to a nested package too, so excluding it would leave its own
# archive empty. It rides in harbor's archive as the example does, and harbor_test/.pubignore
# keeps its build output, lockfile and override out of both.
